// A reflexive claim needs no derivation: the two sides are the same term, so
// `id` closes it in nought steps. That these are provable at all is the price
// of stating them — a corpus proves everything it states — and it is a price
// worth paying to keep `rewrite` addressing one kind of thing.
proof pair_check = id;
proof state_check = id;
proof emit_pre_and_post = id;
